    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93327" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρῑσα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sarissa</i>, a long pike used in
			the Macedonian phalanx, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.12.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.69.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.29.2
			</span></i>, etc. (Freq. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρισσα</span>, Ov<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Metam.</u>
				12.466
			</span></i>, Lucan.<i><span class="en">
				8.298
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρισα</span> appears in most
			of the best codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.69
			</span></i>, etc., and is recognized by Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.267
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
